e_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.04220155372916259,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":29.7,"_gate_insider_own":0.09589,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":63.9,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Miami International Holdings, Inc., through its subsidiaries, builds and operates various financial marketplaces in the United States. It operates through Options, Equities, and International segments. The company's markets include options through MIAX Options, MIAX Pearl, MIAX Emerald, and MIAX Sapphire; U.S. equities through MIAX Pearl Equities; U.S. futures and options on futures through MIAX Futures; and international listings through BSX and TISE. It also trades Hard Red Spring Wheat futures and options on MIAX Futures; provides clearing services for U.S. futures and options on futures through MIAX Futures Clearing; and owns Dorman Trading, a full-service futures commission merchant provides execution and clearing services for introducing brokers, retail customers, institutional clients, and professional traders. In addition, the company offers financial markets and securities services to public and private companies. Miami International Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 2007 and is headquartered in Princeton, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Thomas P. Gallagher Esq. | Chairman & CEO | Age 65 | Compensation: $13.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 439 people. Revenue per employee of $3.1M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $330K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $131K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Miami International Holdings, I is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.4B market cap on $1.4B of annual revenue.","Returns on capital run at 20% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 11-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 32%.","The business throws off $145M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","Accruals are elevated at -18.9% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage runs at 7.1\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 0.6%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 9.6% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.3\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 70% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.6999070286732935},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 22% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.0% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $19.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Hahn Capital Management LLC Makes New $4.49 Million Investment in Miami International Holdings, Inc. $MIAX","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/hahn-capital-management-llc-makes-new-4-49-million-investment-in-miami-international-holdings-inc-miax.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793879025.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.813,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"MIAX Files with the SEC to Offer Cash-settled Binary Index Options and KPI Binary Options on its SEC-registered Exchanges","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/miax-files-with-the-sec-to-offer-cash-settled-binary-index-options-and-kpi-binary-options-on-its-sec-registered-exchanges-302927368.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793706300.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"What Miami International (MIAX) Said on Its Q3 Earnings Call","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/31/what-miami-international-miax-said-on-its-q3-earnings-call.html","date":"2026-10-31","timestamp":1793488376.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.875,"tier":0,"scope":"comp